  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["C8"],
      "pins": [],
      "nets": ["servo power rail (D3 cathode / J10.pin2 / J11.pin2)"],
      "observed": "On the servo power rail downstream of the PMEG3030EP diode, the bulk-capacitor bank is drawn as C4=100u, C2=100u, C6=100u and C8=1000u. C8 is 1000 µF.",
      "expected": "The specification lists the servo-rail bulk bank as 'C1–C4 | 100 µF × 4' — four matched 100 µF capacitors. All four should be 100 µF, not one being 1000 µF.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "C8 1000u (top-right bulk-cap cluster, alongside C4 100u, C2 100u, C6 100u)"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "C1–C4 | 100 µF × 4 | Bulk capacitance on the servo power rail (downstream of D2), buffering the high inrush current of PWM servos."}
      ],
      "impact": "A 1000 µF capacitor (10× the intended value) on the servo rail changes the rail's charge/discharge dynamics: it increases the capacitive inrush at power-on and slows the rail's voltage rise/recovery, which is precisely the inrush condition the matched 100 µF bank was sized to manage. This can make the board behave differently from the reference (e.g. brown-out of the M5Stack on servo startup) and is a deviation from the documented 100 µF × 4 design.",
      "confidence": 0.6
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The schematic is functionally consistent with the spec (diode directions, jumper network, MAX3485 bias values, battery/5V paths all match), but the servo-rail bulk capacitor bank contains one 1000 µF part (C8) where the specification calls for four matched 100 µF capacitors, a 10× value deviation that alters the inrush/decoupling behaviour of the servo supply."
}

